<title>USA: JG Industries posts Q3 loss, sets stock buyback.</title>
<headline>JG Industries posts Q3 loss, sets stock buyback.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>JG Industries Inc said on Tuesday that it lost $309,000 in the third quarter  ended October 26, versus net income of $5.2 million one year ago.</p>
<p>The company said the 1995 figure included a $6.1 million gain from the sale of its Huffman Koos furniture division. Without the sale, the loss in 1995 was $934,000.</p>
<p>JG Industries also said its stockholders approved a plan to repurchase nearly 3.9 million common shares from Jupiter Industries. In return, Jupiter waived payment of accumulated and unpaid dividends of $1.1 million, JG Industries said.</p>
<p>JG Industries is a retail holding company.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
